                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I feel sad to \"not recommend\" this one because this has everything to be a great puzzler. This is MY experience:\n\nLooks-wise, I love it.\nThe concept is actually quite unique, based on node programming. I'm no programmer and the game eased you in on it, it's all about logic after all.\nOutside of the node bits, you can create platforms yourself. It instantly reminded me of those present-day \"Assassin's Creed Revelations\" gameplay bits. Nostalgia ahah.\nNo story whatsoever tho but that's neither here or there.\nSoundtrack is alright, dunno how this one even has it separate from the game but ok, I'll listen to it later I guess.\n\nIt is somewhat challenging at times. I did got stuck on a couple rooms before and managed it... Until I couldn't.\nThe re-spawn system is atrocious, sometimes making you re-start the entire level all over again.\nAnd although moving and connecting a couple nodes around may look cool or fun at the start, it gets trickier.\nEventually, I've reached a certain level, I had no idea where else to go or what to move/edit for far too long.\n\nI feel dumb sometimes, in order to continue you need to keep trying different methods, and that's completely fine, that's how I've solved a few rooms. It did not worked forever, and I am not watching YouTube to continue on.\nMany loved the challenges, some even said they're easy. I guess I'm not that bright lol",
